RDG–GM v2 VISUAL 
--------------------------------
1. Free grade (shape 1)
   c_n(z) = e^(−0.12z)cos(0.7w) + 0.12 − ½
   → baseline backbone law; n is label only.
   → smooth decay + oscillation = unforced grade evolution.

2. Periodic‑in‑n (shape 2)
   c_n(z + n) = c_n(z)
   → introduces grade periodicity (usually rejected).
   → pink waveform shows forced repetition; gold ghost shows free law.

3. Replication / transport (shape 3)
   c_n(w) = 0.85 c_n(w−1) − 0.40 c_n(w−2), w ≥ 2
   → F‑law: later coefficients generated from early seeds.
   → extra structure, not part of backbone.

4. Twist A vs Twist C
   Law A: c^(A)(w) = c(w + k) (K‑shift, suffix operator)
   Law C: c^(C)(w) = c((w + k) mod n) (rejected, not K‑compatible)
   → blue curve = accepted suffix shift;
     red curve = excluded periodic wrap.

Axes:
   horizontal: grade axis z = w − 1
   vertical: ℜ c (real part of coefficient)
